# WolkaraForever layer patch 0080 - host: TouchPlay's buttons take their fingers (iPad touch)
#
# Why: in iPad touch the TouchPlay add-on draws the game's touch buttons and saves where they are and
# which CTRL-ALT-SHIFT keys they have (the contract, TouchContract.h). The layer's AKTouchAreas
# (TouchAreas.m) turns a finger on one of them into its keys and draws the press glow and hold ring;
# this patch is the host's half:
#   - In iPad touch only, the host view makes the areas, gives them its key path and keeps them told of
#     its fingers: every touches* method offers its fingers to the areas first, and a finger the areas
#     take never reaches the 1.0.8 direct-touch gestures (0055) or the trackpad. With no contract the
#     areas take nothing, so the host is exactly what it was. Every other mode makes no areas.
#   - A key with modifiers: the host's only key calls (0059's touchKey:characters:pressed: and
#     touchSpecialKey:) post modifierFlags 0. touchKey:characters:modifiers:pressed: presses each
#     modifier the key needs (a flags-changed event with that modifier's key code and left-hand bit, as
#     a Mac keyboard reports it), posts the key, and releases those modifiers in reverse - for the down
#     and again for the up, so nothing is held between two touch keys.
#   - A finger that ends while another is held on a button still finishes the direct gesture: the
#     "is any other finger of this gesture down" check skips the buttons' fingers.
#   - The pinch recognizer never takes a finger on a button (a spell plus a walk is not a pinch).
#   - "Touch buttons not found" (touch.contract.missing) is shown once per game start in the game view
#     when iPad touch has no contract, once the view has a size.
#   - When the view changes size (rotation, Stage Manager) the areas let go of every finger, as the
#     toolbar does: a held Jump key is released and no finger keeps an old rectangle.
#
# Applies after: 0079-host-gate-follows-the-interface-mode.patch
# Applies to: translation/AppKit/AppKit.m
# Upstream: no (TouchPlay and iPad touch live in the WolkaraForever layer).
#
